Lab 4: Access Virtual Machines via Web Console
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Launch virtual machines using the OpenShift web console interface
Access VM consoles through VNC (Virtual Network Computing) connections
Manage virtual machine lifecycle using OpenShift CLI tools
Navigate between web-based and command-line VM management approaches
Troubleshoot common VM console access issues
Understand the relationship between OpenShift Virtualization and traditional VM management
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command-line operations
Familiarity with OpenShift concepts and navigation
Knowledge of virtual machine fundamentals
Access to an OpenShift cluster with OpenShift Virtualization operator installed
Basic understanding of YAML configuration files
Familiarity with kubectl/oc command-line tools
