Task 3: Use CLI Tools to Start and Stop the VM
Subtask 3.1: VM Management with OpenShift CLI
List Virtual Machines

# List all VMs in current namespace
oc get vm

# Get detailed information about VMs
oc get vm -o wide

# Describe specific VM
oc describe vm lab4-test-vm
Check VM Status

# Check VM instance status
oc get vmi

# Get detailed VM instance information
oc get vmi lab4-test-vm -o yaml

# Check VM events
oc get events --field-selector involvedObject.name=lab4-test-vm
Subtask 3.2: VM Lifecycle Management with virtctl
Install and Verify virtctl (if not already available)

# Check if virtctl is installed
which virtctl

# If not installed, download it
# Note: In the lab environment, virtctl should already be available
virtctl version
Stop the Virtual Machine

# Stop VM using virtctl
virtctl stop lab4-test-vm

# Verify VM is stopped
oc get vm lab4-test-vm

# Check that VMI is terminated
oc get vmi
Start the Virtual Machine

# Start VM using virtctl
virtctl start lab4-test-vm

# Monitor startup process
oc get vm lab4-test-vm -w

# Verify VM is running
oc get vmi lab4-test-vm
Subtask 3.3: Advanced CLI Operations
Restart Virtual Machine

# Restart VM (stop and start)
virtctl restart lab4-test-vm

# Force restart if needed
virtctl restart lab4-test-vm --force
Pause and Unpause VM

# Pause VM execution
virtctl pause vmi lab4-test-vm

# Check paused status
oc get vmi lab4-test-vm -o jsonpath='{.status.phase}'

# Unpause VM
virtctl unpause vmi lab4-test-vm
Access VM via CLI Console

# Connect to VM console via CLI
virtctl console lab4-test-vm

# To exit console, use: Ctrl+] or type 'exit'

# Connect with VNC viewer
virtctl vnc lab4-test-vm
Subtask 3.4: VM Resource Monitoring
Monitor VM Resources

# Check VM resource usage
oc top vmi

# Get detailed resource information
oc get vmi lab4-test-vm -o jsonpath='{.status.guestOSInfo}'

# Check VM conditions
oc get vmi lab4-test-vm -o jsonpath='{.status.conditions[*].type}'
View VM Logs

# Get VM-related pod logs
oc get pods -l kubevirt.io/vm=lab4-test-vm

# View virt-launcher pod logs
oc logs -l kubevirt.io/vm=lab4-test-vm
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Console Access Problems
VNC Console Not Loading

# Check VM status
oc get vm lab4-test-vm
oc get vmi lab4-test-vm

# Verify VM is running
oc describe vmi lab4-test-vm

# Check for errors in events
oc get events --sort-by='.lastTimestamp'
Console Connection Timeout

Verify network connectivity
Check browser security settings
Try different browser or incognito mode
Ensure WebSocket connections are allowed
CLI Command Issues
virtctl Command Not Found

# Check if virtctl is in PATH
echo $PATH

# Find virtctl location
find /usr -name virtctl 2>/dev/null

# Use oc plugin if virtctl not available
oc plugin list | grep virt
Permission Denied Errors

# Check current user permissions
oc auth can-i create vm
oc auth can-i get vmi

# Verify project access
oc project
oc get rolebindings
VM Startup Issues
VM Fails to Start
# Check VM configuration
oc get vm lab4-test-vm -o yaml

# Look for error conditions
oc describe vm lab4-test-vm

# Check resource availability
oc describe nodes
